name    sddemo
prog    sddemo
# White's Speedisk 2.10, the demo: it reads the volume, draws a block map of
# it, and offers a menu -- Optimize, Change drive, Rescan, Disk statistics,
# Exit -- with a legend for the four block kinds.
#
# NOTHING HERE PRESSES OPTIMIZE, and that is deliberate: this is a
# defragmenter and the disk it would rewrite is the collection.  Measured
# before this was written (2026-09-21): a copy of the image was md5'd,
# sddemo was left drawing for thirty seconds, and the md5 was unchanged --
# so CAPTURING it costs nothing.  That says nothing at all about Optimize,
# which nobody has run and which this test must not.  The shipped image was
# md5'd again after this test and was likewise unchanged.
#
# NO KEYS ARE SENT EITHER, and that is measurement rather than caution: the
# status panel still reads `Analyzing...' at forty seconds on a 312M image,
# so `d' and `e' were ignored and the snaps taken after them were the same
# screen under a different name.  A snap named `stats' holding the map is
# the shape that put a wrong line on dm's card, so it is not repeated here.
rate    0.8
size    24 80
wait    40
snap    map
expect  Speedisk
expect  E)xit Speedisk
expect  Used Block
